INT. WEDDING PLANNER'S OFFICE - DAY

Swatches pinned to corkboards. A mood board shaped like a heart. A cold cappuccino. On the desk, an old desk phone with a red blinking light.

BEATRIX LOMBARDI, thirties, a wedding planner in a pastel blazer, stares at the phone. Opposite her, NATHANIEL "NAT" OSEI-WRIGHT, thirties, groom, sits upright, hands clamped on his knees. His fiancee's mother, MRS. GENEVIEVE ABARCA, is on the speakerphone.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
(from phone)
Beatrix? Is Nathaniel there? I want him to hear this.

Beatrix gives Nat a tight smile. He nods, the way a man nods when he is being led to a dentist.

BEATRIX
He's right here, Mrs. Abarca.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
Lovely. Nathaniel, dear.

NAT
Hello, Mrs. Abarca.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
I've been thinking about the flowers.

Nat closes his eyes. Beatrix sets her pen down, then picks it up again.

BEATRIX
The peonies?

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
No, no, the peonies are fine. It's the carnations I don't care for.

BEATRIX
We don't have carnations.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
Well, you should.

Beatrix looks at the ceiling. Nat looks at her. A very long pause stretches.

NAT
(carefully)
Mrs. Abarca, I think carnations are a terrific idea.

BEATRIX
(sharp, aside)
Nat.

NAT
(aside)
What? It's a flower.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
You see? Nathaniel understands. Beatrix, I want carnations on every table, and on the cake, and in the bride's hair.

BEATRIX
In her hair.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
Is there a problem?

BEATRIX
None at all.

Beatrix pushes a notepad toward Nat. He picks up a pen and writes: SAY NO. Beatrix reads it, nods, and writes beneath it: YOU SAY NO. Nat reads it, shakes his head violently, and underlines his own: SAY NO.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
Hello? Did I lose you?

NAT
No. We're here.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
I wanted to ask one more thing.

BEATRIX
(through her teeth)
Of course.

GENEVIEVE (V.O.)
Is it too late to change the date?

Nat drops his pen. Beatrix stands. She goes to the phone, lifts the handset, hangs up on Mrs. Abarca, and sets the receiver down with immense care. The red light stops blinking.

Neither of them speaks. Nat folds the notepad in half, and in half again, and tucks it into his breast pocket.

NAT
Carnations.

BEATRIX
Carnations.

She sits back down and takes a long sip of the cold cappuccino.
